{
  // Formatted the way `next build` writes it, on purpose.
  //
  // Next 16 rewrites this file on every build: it expands the arrays, sets
  // "jsx" to "react-jsx", and adds the .next/dev/types include. When the
  // committed file said something else, every console build left a dirty
  // tree, and four agents reverted the identical diff by hand in one day. The
  // fifth would have committed it as their own change, and the sixth would
  // have spent an afternoon on why the committed config disagreed with the
  // tool. Committing what the tool writes makes the build a no-op here
  // instead, verified rather than assumed: two consecutive builds leave the
  // file byte identical and `tsc --noEmit` is clean against it.
  //
  // Why four people met this and described it four different ways: it is Next
  // 16 behaviour and a stale Next 15 install does not do it at all. Every
  // report was accurate about the tree it was made in. The variable none of
  // them could see was inside their own node_modules, which is why this looked
  // like flakiness and was not. Run `npm ci` before concluding anything here.
  //
  // Comments do survive the rewrite, which is why this one can be here.
  "compilerOptions": {
    "target": "ES2022",
    "lib": [
      "dom",
      "dom.iterable",
      "esnext"
    ],
    "allowJs": true,
    "skipLibCheck": true,
    "strict": true,
    "noEmit": true,
    "esModuleInterop": true,
    "module": "esnext",
    "moduleResolution": "bundler",
    "resolveJsonModule": true,
    "isolatedModules": true,
    // node --test runs lib/*.test.ts directly through type stripping, which
    // needs the real specifier including its extension. Legal here only
    // because noEmit is set: nothing is written, so nothing can emit an import
    // of a file that will not exist. Verified against the rewrite this file
    // documents, two consecutive next builds leave it byte identical.
    "allowImportingTsExtensions": true,
    "jsx": "react-jsx",
    "incremental": true,
    "plugins": [
      {
        "name": "next"
      }
    ],
    "paths": {
      "@/*": [
        "./*"
      ]
    }
  },
  "include": [
    "next-env.d.ts",
    "**/*.ts",
    "**/*.tsx",
    ".next/types/**/*.ts",
    ".next/dev/types/**/*.ts"
  ],
  "exclude": [
    "node_modules"
  ]
}
